course: dictionary
lesson: 13594
title: Inconstant: changing and unreliable
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Inconstant is a word you will meet in old stories, poems and formal writing. It is made of in- (not) and constant (staying the same), so it means not staying the same. «The inconstant moon» in an old poem changes shape every night. Look at the word's parts, then check the meaning in the sentence.
explain: Inconstant can describe a person. «Dan was an inconstant friend: he was kind on Monday and ignored me on Friday.» Dan is not loyal or faithful, because the way he treats his friend keeps changing.
explain: It can also describe things that change in amount or strength. «The inconstant wind blew hard, then died away, then blew hard again.» The wind is not steady. In everyday talk, people say changeable or unreliable instead, so you will hear those words more often.
fact: Inconstant means changing often, or not steady.
fact: Inconstant can describe a person who is not loyal or faithful, such as an inconstant friend.
fact: Inconstant can describe weather, wind or amounts that keep changing, such as inconstant weather.
fact: The «inconstant moon» is an old poetry phrase for the moon, which changes shape each night.
fact: Inconstant is mostly found in stories, poems and formal writing. Everyday words for it are changeable and unreliable.
exercise: «The inconstant wind blew hard, then died away.» What does inconstant mean here? | Always the same | *Not steady, changing in strength | Quiet and calm | Very cold
exercise: Sam keeps changing how he treats Ella: kind one day, cold the next. What does inconstant suggest about Sam? | *Changing often, not loyal | Very tall | Always loyal and faithful | Sleepy after school
exercise: Which everyday word means nearly the same as inconstant? | Bright | Ancient | *Changeable | Steady
test: «The inconstant moon» is a phrase from old poems. What does inconstant mean in it? | *The moon changes shape, so it is not steady | The moon is made of cheese | The moon is very far away | The moon is always full
test: Which sentence uses inconstant correctly? | *The inconstant weather changed from sunshine to rain to snow in one afternoon | Her inconstant shoes were very warm | The inconstant book had a happy ending | The river was inconstant, always running at exactly the same speed
exam: Read «My cousin is an inconstant friend: she laughs with me one day and avoids me the next.» What is the best meaning of inconstant? | *Changes often, not reliable | Loyal and always there | Very funny | Very angry
